00:05:07,199 --> 00:05:13,199
Think fast. Look alive. Die hard.

2
00:10:14,399 --> 00:10:20,399
Die Hard: With a Vengeance is a action, thriller
film directed by John McTiernan.

3
00:15:21,599 --> 00:15:27,599
New York detective John McClane is back and kicking bad-guy butt in the third installment of this action-packed
series, which finds him teaming with civilian Zeus Carver to prevent the loss of innocent lives.

4
00:20:28,799 --> 00:20:34,799
McClane thought he'd seen it all, until a genius named Simon engages McClane, his new "partner"
-- and his beloved city -- in a deadly game that demands their concentration.

5
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:42,000
John McClane, played by Bruce Willis.

6
00:30:43,199 --> 00:30:49,199
Zeus Carver, played by Samuel L. Jackson.

7
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:56,400
Simon, played by Jeremy Irons.

8
00:40:57,599 --> 00:41:03,599
Chief Walter Cobb, played by Larry Bryggman.

9
00:46:04,799 --> 00:46:10,799
Joe Lambert, played by Graham Greene.

10
00:51:12,000 --> 00:51:18,000
Ricky Walsh, played by Anthony Peck.

11
00:56:19,199 --> 00:56:25,199
Die Hard with a Vengeance is a 1995 American action film directed and produced by John
McTiernan, written by Jonathan Hensleigh, and starring Bruce Willis as John McClane.

12
01:01:26,399 --> 01:01:32,399
It is the sequel to Die Hard (1988) and Die Hard 2 (1990) and the
third installment in the Die Hard film series.

13
01:06:33,599 --> 01:06:39,599
The film also stars Jeremy Irons and Samuel L.

14
01:11:40,800 --> 01:11:46,800
Jackson, and features Graham Greene, Colleen Camp,
Larry Bryggman and Sam Phillips.

15
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:54,000
In the film, NYPD Lieutenant John McClane is embroiled in a plot by a mysterious terrorist calling himself “Simon” (Irons), who extorts the
city of New York by threatening to detonate several bombs unless McClane solves a series of games scattered across the city.

16
01:21:55,199 --> 01:22:01,199
McClane reluctantly partners with a shopkeeper named Zeus Carver (Jackson), and learns the
terrorists plot to steal the gold bullion of the Federal Reserve Bank of New York.

17
01:27:02,399 --> 01:27:08,399
Adapted from a spec script written by Hensleigh, Die Hard with a Vengeance was the first film in the series not directly based on a literary source material, and
the first not to be produced by Joel Silver and Lawrence Gordon after both producers had a fall-out with Willis, instead being produced by Andrew G.

18
01:32:09,599 --> 01:32:15,599
Vajna’s Cinergi Pictures.

19
01:37:16,800 --> 01:37:22,800
Principal photography took place in New York City and South Carolina.

20
01:42:24,000 --> 01:42:30,000
The film was released on May 19, 1995 by 20th Century Fox and grossed $366.1 million worldwide, becoming
the highest-grossing film of the year, and initially received mixed reviews from critics.

21
01:47:31,199 --> 01:47:37,199
However, the film has received positive reevaluation over time and is
now largely considered the best sequel in the franchise.

22
01:52:38,399 --> 01:52:44,399
The film was followed by Live Free or Die Hard in 2007
and A Good Day to Die Hard in 2013.

23
01:57:45,599 --> 01:57:51,599
The film explores themes of new york city, taxi, gold, helicopter, robbery.

24
02:02:52,799 --> 02:02:58,799
The tone is intense.
